        <mxCell id="e43" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="a9" target="ba9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note" value="Notes&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Rejections before &quot;Store callback data&quot; never modify the payment, so a forged or repeated callback cannot corrupt it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Failures are saved and a result is returned, never thrown: a throw would roll back the save.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Verifying is saved &lt;b&gt;before&lt;/b&gt; the verify call. A timeout leaves it Verifying for a later inquiry job (not built yet).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; The amount in the verify response is authoritative; the callback amount is only an early check.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Each PSP adapter turns its own callback form into a PSP-neutral PspCallback; only RawStatus/RawStatusCode keep the PSP's own values.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; If the reverse request itself fails, the payment stays Verifying and the user sees the pending page.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Succeeded and both ledger entries are saved in one transaction.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; The callback is a browser navigation, so a server-side 302 to the client result page is correct here." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="2220" width="1480" height="190" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
